nub-sandbox

The macOS Seatbelt essential base profile
(src/backend/macos_seatbelt_base.sbpl) and the glob→Seatbelt-regex translation
(glob_to_seatbelt_regex in src/backend/macos.rs) are adapted from OpenAI Codex
(https://github.com/openai/codex), licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

    Copyright OpenAI
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Codex's Seatbelt base policy is itself derived from the Chromium project's macOS
sandbox policy (https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src), licensed
under the BSD 3-Clause License:

    Copyright The Chromium Authors
    Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.

The Linux backend launches an UNMODIFIED upstream Bubblewrap executable. Release
builds package that executable — statically linked against libcap and musl — as
a fallback resource (bin/nub-resources), built by scripts/build-bwrap-resource.sh
from pinned, checksum-verified upstream releases. No source of any of the three is
modified.

    bubblewrap 0.11.2 (https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap)
    Copyright the bubblewrap authors.
    Its license text ships in the resource bundle as COPYING.bubblewrap, and the
    complete corresponding source ships alongside it as
    bubblewrap-0.11.2.tar.xz.

    libcap 2.78 (https://sites.google.com/site/fullycapable/)
    Copyright Andrew G. Morgan and contributors.
    Its license text ships in the resource bundle as LICENSE.libcap, and the
    complete corresponding source ships alongside it as libcap-2.78.tar.xz.

    musl libc 1.2.5 (https://musl.libc.org/)
    Copyright Rich Felker and contributors.
    Its license text ships in the resource bundle as COPYRIGHT.musl.

Consult each upstream project for its authoritative license terms; the texts
above are shipped verbatim rather than restated here.
